{
 "_comment": "Past crates and boxes and what each held, for the Past tab. Hand-maintained: names (matched to catalogue items by name) and the listed drop rates, as supplied by the user. `items: []` with `pending: true` means the contents have not been added yet (a placeholder, not an empty box). A hair/face entry needs `kind` and `gender`. build-catalog.mjs resolves the names into catalog.boxes and warns about any it cannot find. `pill` is the short name shown on the box's pill (omit it for an unnamed box: the pill then shows just the dates); `name` is the full name shown above the contents. Sources (saved Nexon cash shop update pages, 29/10/2026 and 04/11/2026): Founder's crate, Aurora crate and the Oct 6 Mystery Styles from the Grand Launch page; Mystery Fashion Crate (Oct 21) and Halloween crate and the Oct 28 Mystery Styles from the Oct 28 page; Mystery Fashion Crate (Nov 4) from the Nov 4 page. An `end` with no time (the Nov 4 crate: \"Wednesday, November 18 (Start of Maintenance)\") counts as a whole UTC day: on sale to the end of that day, shown as a date and days left, never an hour. Only these boxes are listed: pets, packs, megaphones, 10-day equip covers, Signature coupons and other shop items are not. Rates are only known for the Halloween crate (supplied by the user); the pages link to the rates but do not print them. The post corrected the female Oct 28 hair list: Cecelia Twist, not Rockstar Hair. `match` on an item is the catalogue name to look for when the box's name differs (the game's hair names carry a colour prefix: Black Wild Tangles Hair, Black Romantic Braid Hair). `latest: true` marks the newest box, which the Released tab always opens on. A group's `tab` is the short label on its tab (the Released tab shows tabs, not the long `title`). `start` and `end` (UTC, ISO) are the times the Nexon update pages print for each box: the pages print the last minute (7:59 AM), so the box is on rotation up to and including that minute. A start with no time (2026-10-06, 2026-10-21) is a date only: the pages say \"End of Maintenance\" and \"Start of Grand Launch\" without a time. The page uses them for the On rotation / Out of rotation labels.",
